===Climate===
[[File:Okayama Mikan Orchard.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Mikan orchards on the southern coast of Sanzu, with the Shendan Ocean visible beyond the terraces.]]

Okayama Prefecture experiences a humid subtropical climate (Köppen climate classification ''Cfa''), moderated by the surrounding ocean on three sides. The maritime influence produces warm, relatively mild winters and hot, humid summers, with the ocean currents that wrap around the peninsula creating a frost-free growing season that is among the longest in Okaiken. This climate is the foundation of the prefecture's citrus industry — the warm, stable temperatures and absence of killing frosts allow citrus to ripen fully on the tree, developing the exceptional sweetness for which Okayama mikan is known.

The eastern coast, facing the Sanzu Inland Sea toward Shiogami, is more sheltered from typhoons than the southern coast, which is exposed to storms sweeping up from the Yagikoshu mainland. The mountainous interior receives the highest precipitation, with annual totals exceeding 2,400 mm in the Tsurugi district.

